 # @acme/ui
 
-Accessible React components.
+Accessible React components (React 19), style-agnostic: no CSS and no class names are imposed. Pass `className` and any other DOM props; they land on the root element of each component. Ids come from `React.useId`, so several instances can share a page.
+
+Components: `Tabs`, `Dialog`, `Combobox`. They follow the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices patterns for tabs, modal dialogs and combobox with listbox popup.
+
+## Development
+
+- `pnpm test` runs the Vitest suite (jsdom + Testing Library).
+- `pnpm typecheck` runs `tsc --noEmit`.
+
+## Tabs
+
+```tsx
+import { Tab, TabList, TabPanel, Tabs } from "@acme/ui";
+
+<Tabs defaultValue="profile">
+  <TabList aria-label="Account">
+    <Tab value="profile">Profile</Tab>
+    <Tab value="billing" disabled>Billing</Tab>
+    <Tab value="security">Security</Tab>
+  </TabList>
+  <TabPanel value="profile">Profile settings</TabPanel>
+  <TabPanel value="billing">Billing settings</TabPanel>
+  <TabPanel value="security">Security settings</TabPanel>
+</Tabs>;
+```
+
+Selection is uncontrolled by default. Pass `value` with `onValueChange` for controlled use; a parent that ignores the callback keeps the previous tab. When the requested tab is missing or disabled, the first enabled tab is selected.
+
+### Tabs props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `defaultValue` | `string` | first enabled tab | Initially selected tab (uncontrolled). |
+| `value` | `string` | — | Selected tab (controlled). Wins over `defaultValue`. |
+| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` | — | Called on every user selection change. Not called when the selected tab is chosen again. |
+
+Other `div` props are passed to the root element.
+
+### TabList props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `aria-label` | `string` | — | Accessible name. Required unless `aria-labelledby` is given. |
+| `aria-labelledby` | `string` | — | Id of the element that names the list. |
+
+Other `div` props are passed to the `role="tablist"` element. `onKeyDown` is called before the built-in handling.
+
+### Tab props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` | — | Identifies the tab and its panel. Required. |
+| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables the tab: it cannot be clicked, selected or reached with arrow keys. `aria-disabled="true"` has the same effect. |
+
+Other `button` props are passed to the `role="tab"` button.
+
+### TabPanel props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` | — | The tab this panel belongs to. Required. |
+
+Inactive panels are rendered with `hidden`. Other `div` props are passed through.
+
+### Tabs keyboard
+
+| Key | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| Tab | Moves focus into the selected tab, then into its panel. Only the selected tab is in the tab order. |
+| ArrowRight | Moves to the next enabled tab, wrapping from the last to the first. Selects it. |
+| ArrowLeft | Moves to the previous enabled tab, wrapping from the first to the last. Selects it. |
+| Home | Moves to the first enabled tab and selects it. |
+| End | Moves to the last enabled tab and selects it. |
+
+Arrow and Home/End keys call `preventDefault`. Tab order follows the DOM order of the tabs, so tabs added or removed later are handled.
+
+## Dialog
+
+```tsx
+import { Dialog } from "@acme/ui";
+
+<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} title="Delete project" description="This cannot be undone.">
+  <button type="button" onClick={remove}>Delete</button>
+</Dialog>;
+```
+
+The dialog renders nothing while `open` is false. When open it is rendered into `document.body` through a portal, with a backdrop element around `role="dialog"`. Focus moves to the first tabbable element inside (or to the dialog itself if there is none), Tab and Shift+Tab cycle within the dialog, and focus returns to the previously focused element when the dialog closes or unmounts.
+
+Dialogs nest. Open dialogs form a stack ordered by nesting depth, so a dialog rendered inside another is always above it, even when both mount open in the same render. Escape closes only the top-most dialog, and Tab and focus stay within it, so an inner dialog never closes or hands focus to the outer one.
+
+### Dialog props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `open` | `boolean` | — | Whether the dialog is shown. Required. |
+| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` | — | Called with `false` on Escape or a backdrop click. Required. |
+| `title` | `ReactNode` | — | Rendered in an `h2`; labels the dialog. Required. |
+| `description` | `ReactNode` | — | Rendered in a `p`; describes the dialog. When omitted, `aria-describedby` is absent. |
+| `children` | `ReactNode` | — | Dialog content. |
+
+`className` and other `div` props are passed to the `role="dialog"` element. The backdrop element has a `data-backdrop` attribute for styling.
+
+### Dialog keyboard and pointer
+
+| Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| Escape | Calls `onOpenChange(false)` on the top-most dialog, unless an inner component already handled the key (`defaultPrevented`). A nested `Combobox` consumes Escape while its list is open. Escape in an inner dialog does not close the outer one. |
+| Tab | Moves to the next tabbable element; from the last, wraps to the first. |
+| Shift+Tab | Moves to the previous tabbable element; from the first, wraps to the last. |
+| Click on backdrop | Calls `onOpenChange(false)` when the press and the release both happen on the backdrop. A press that starts inside the dialog and ends on the backdrop does not close it. |
+| Click inside | Does not close the dialog. |
+
+Tabbable elements exclude disabled elements, elements with `tabindex` below 0, and hidden inputs. The list is computed at each keypress, so content added after opening is included.
+
+## Combobox
+
+```tsx
+import { Combobox, type ComboboxOption } from "@acme/ui";
+
+const fruits: ComboboxOption<string>[] = [
+  { value: "apple", label: "Apple" },
+  { value: "kiwi", label: "Kiwi", disabled: true },
+];
+
+<Combobox label="Fruit" options={fruits} placeholder="Search fruit" onChange={(value) => setFruit(value)} />;
+```
+
+Use a generic type for other value types, for example `Combobox<number>`; `onChange` then receives `number | null`.
+
+Typing filters the options by case-insensitive substring match. Regex characters are matched literally, and an empty or whitespace-only query shows all options. Typing that empties the input leaves no option active; ArrowDown then activates the first enabled option, and ArrowUp the last.
+
+### Combobox props
+
+| Name | Type | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `label` | `string` | — | Visible label for the input. Also names the listbox. Required. |
+| `options` | `ComboboxOption<T>[]` | — | `{ value, label, disabled? }` entries. Required. |
+| `value` | `T \| null` | — | Selected option value (controlled). `null` means no selection. |
+| `defaultValue` | `T \| null` | `null` | Initial selection (uncontrolled). |
+| `onChange` | `(value: T \| null) => void` | — | Called when an option is chosen, or with `null` when the text is cleared and the input loses focus (or Enter is pressed with empty text). |
+| `placeholder` | `string` | — | Placeholder for the input. |
+
+`T` is `string | number` and defaults to `string`. The value `0` is a real value. Other `div` props are passed to the root element.
+
+### Combobox keyboard
+
+| Key | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| ArrowDown | Opens the list if closed (activating the first enabled option). Otherwise moves the active option to the next enabled option, wrapping from the last to the first. |
+| ArrowUp | Opens the list if closed (activating the last enabled option). Otherwise moves to the previous enabled option, wrapping from the first to the last. |
+| Enter | With an active option: selects it, closes the list and shows its label. With no active option: does nothing, unless the text is empty and a value is selected, which clears the selection (`onChange(null)`). |
+| Escape | While the list is open: closes it without selecting and restores the selected label. Stops propagation, so an enclosing `Dialog` stays open. |
+| Typing | Opens the list and filters the options. |
+| Blur | Closes the list and restores the selected label. If the text is empty and a value was selected, calls `onChange(null)`. |
+
+Focus stays on the input throughout. The active option is exposed through `aria-activedescendant`, which is absent when no option is active. Disabled options are skipped by the arrow keys, and clicking one does nothing. A click on an enabled option selects it. When nothing matches, the list shows a "No results" status message.
